    "result_text": "The full build passes. The suite ran green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe business-day roll for owner registration dates now skips public holidays as well as weekends. The rule lives in one place \u2014 `BusinessDays.rollForward` \u2014 which both `ResolveOwnerRegistrationDate` (stamping the owner) and `RejectDailyOwnerLimit` (via the published resolved date) already share, so a date and the day it's counted against continue to roll identically.\n\nChange in `BusinessDays.java`:\n- Added the fixed holiday set (`2026-01-01, 2026-01-26, 2026-04-25, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-28`).\n- Extended the roll loop to also advance when the date lands on a listed holiday, extracting the weekend check into a small `isWeekend` helper to keep the loop condition readable.\n\nNo other class needed changes \u2014 the logic stayed in the single unit responsible for defining a business day.",
